  "raw_text": "57\n\nDaiwan taya saika dadingkra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \ntanner\n \n/ curtidor\n\nDaiwan tim\n \n(a/t:\n \nDaiwan tem\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ndomesticated (tame) animal\n \n/ animal domesticado\n\nDaiwan tnawira\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbird\n \n/ pájaro\n\nDaiwan wail\n \n(a/t:\n \nwaild\n-\ndict\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nwild animal\n \n/ animal salvaje\n\nDâkaia\n \n(Dakaia)\n \n(a/t:\n \nDakaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto harvest, to reap\n \n/ cosechar\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nMâ krikaia, Insla krikaia, Insla\ndâkaia\n)\n\nDâkaia warkka tatakra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nharvest worker\n \n/ trabajador de la cosecha\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb78\n):\n \nJehova ra puram suns dâkaia warkka tatakra nani kau blîkbia dukiara\n \n–\n \nPray to Jehovah to send more\nharvest workers\n \n/ Oren a Jehová para que envíe más trabajadores de la cosecha)\n\nInsla dâkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto harvest, to reap\n \n/ cosechar\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nMâ krikaia, Insla krikaia, Dâkaia\n)\n\nDakakaia\n \n(v-trans)\n \n–\n \nto feed, to give a drink, to nourish\n \n/ alimentar, dar de beber, nutrir\n\nPlun dakakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto feed\n \n/ alimentar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-12/18\n):\n \nAlmuk nani ba spirit lainka ra sîp nani ra plun dakakisa, kaina kahbisa bara main kaikisa.\n \n–\n \nElders\nfeed the sheep spiritually, protect, and care for (them).\n \n/ Los ancianos alimentan a las ovejas espiritualmente, las\nprotegen y las cuidan.)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb92\n):\n \nSîpka nani ra plun dakaks\n \n–\n \nFeed my little sheep\n \n/ Alimenta a mis ovejitas)\n\nSîka dakakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto give medicine\n \n/ dar medicina\n\nTiala dakakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto nurse, to breastfeed\n \n/ amamantar\n\nDakawa\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nDikwa\n\nDakbaia\n \n(v-trans; instrans:\n \nDakwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto break, to separate into parts, to take away, to part, to separate, to amputate,\nto cut off, to capture\n \n/ romper, separar en partes, quitar, separar, amputar, cortar, capturar\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb16\n):\n \nSut mihta daks, bara kau mamyunbia apia.\n \n–\n \nTake away all and he will no longer worship you.\n \n/ Quítate todo y él ya\nno te adorará.)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb28\n):\n \nBalac, Moab kingka ba, sibrin kan Israel uplika nani ba ai tasbaya dakbia.\n \n–\n \nBalak, the king of Moab, was scared that\nthe Israelites would take away his land.\n \n/ Balac, el rey de Moab, tenía miedo de que los israelitas le quitaran su tierra.)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nth-5\n):\n \nBîla wala kum dingkpara, baku sin bîla kum dakbaia apia sa\n \n–\n \nDo not insert another word, likewise, we must not take\naway a word\n \n/ No inserte otra palabra, del mismo modo, no debemos quitar una palabra)\n\nAihka aihka dakbaia\n \n(v-trans; intrans:\n \nAihka aihka dakwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto separate, to disperse\n \n/ apartar, separar,\ndispersar\n\nBîla dakbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto interrupt, to cut someone off when speaking\n \n/ interrumpir, interrumpir a alguien cuando\nhabla\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf-23\n):\n \nLuhpiam ba dîa dîa mai aisabia sin, witin bîla dakpara bara praut takpara\n \n–\n \nRegardless of what your child\nsays to you, do not interrupt them and do not get angry\n \n/ Independientemente de lo que le diga su hijo, no lo interrumpa\ny no se enoje)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf-10\n):\n \nMayam ba turi main aisi kabia taim, witin bîla dakpara\n \n–\n \nWhen your mate talks to you, do not interrupt\nthem\n \n/ Cuando tu compañero te hable, no lo interrumpas)\n\n(Note/Nota\n: As seen in the above examples, the “b” is dropped in the prohibitive form of the verb.\n \n/ Como se ve en los\nejemplos anteriores, la \"b\" se elimina en la forma prohibitiva del verbo.)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-04/19\n):\n \nWitin nani aisisa taim, pain wali bîla dakbaia apia\n \n–\n \nWhen they are speaking, listen without\ninterrupting\n \n/ Cuando están hablando, escuchen sin interrumpir)\n\nDakbi briaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto steal, to usurp, to capture\n \n/ robar, usurpar, capturar\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb55\n):\n \nAsiria kingka lâka ba Israel kiamka 10 kingka lâka ba dakbi brin kan\n \n–\n \nThe Assyrian kingdom has captured\nthe Israelite 10 tribe kingdom\n \n/ El reino asirio ha capturado el reino de las 10 tribus israelita)\n\nDakbi dakbi\n \n(adv)\n \n–\n \nseparately\n \n/ por separado\n\nDakbi sakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto separate, to subtract\n \n/ separar, restar\n\nDakbi pri sakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto rescue and free\n \n/ rescatar y liberar\n\nKaina dakbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto hinder, to prevent, to intercept, to impede, to get in front of, to cut off, to contradict\n \n/\nobstaculizar, prevenir, interceptar, impedir, ponerse delante, cortar, contradecir\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-03/20\n):\n \nDîa mita upla kum kum tahbi daukan lâka ba kaina dakbisa ki?\n \n–\n \nWhat might prevent some people\nfrom getting baptized?\n \n/ ¿Qué podría evitar que algunas personas se bauticen?)\n\nMihta dakbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto take from the hand, to deprive of, to take away from, to hold back from\n \n/ tomar de la\nmano, privar, quitar, retener\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh30\n):\n \ndiara pain nani ai uplika mihta dakbisa\n \n–\n \nhe holds back good things from his people\n \n/ él retiene cosas buenas\nde su gente)",
